<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MauiReference.Pages.GapEventAttributePage" Title="Gap: Event Attribute">
    <!-- P3 gap probe: an inline event attribute (Clicked="..."). AUTHORING.md rule 3 bans these in
         shared/tier-1 pages because the port hydrates a static tree with no event-attribute support; this
         tier-2 gap page pins that exact limitation deliberately, per rule 6. Verified: xaml_loader::
         load_into throws "Cannot assign property 'Clicked': Property does not exist" — Clicked is
         rejected as an unrecognized property, not silently ignored. This page IS run through `e2e.py
         gen`/`lint`: both carve it out BY NAME (lint's EVENT_RE check, and gen's STATIC_CHECK_EXEMPT,
         which omits the MAUI_XAML_REJECT_EVENT_ATTRIBUTES static_assert that would otherwise make this
         page un-compilable). The gallery host degrades instead, via xaml_load_options::exception_handler.
         GapEventAttributePage.xaml.cs is hand-written (has OnClicked) so real MAUI still renders +
         behaves correctly (the acceptance gate). -->
    <VerticalStackLayout Margin="12" Spacing="8">
        <Label Text="Gap probe: Clicked=&quot;OnClicked&quot; event attribute" />
        <Button Text="Click me" Clicked="OnClicked" />
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
